# NEITHER DATABASE IS IGNORED. Do not add activity_logs.db or token_usage.db
# back to this file.
#
# That looks backwards — they are runtime data and must never be committed —
# but ignoring a file is exactly what makes git willing to destroy it. Git
# silently overwrites an *ignored* file when a checkout wants to write one
# there, and refuses outright for an untracked-and-unignored one:
#
#   ignored      git checkout <sha that tracks it>  ->  silently clobbered
#   not ignored  git checkout <sha that tracks it>  ->  "would be overwritten
#                                                        by checkout. Aborting"
#
# Eleven commits in this repository's history still track an old copy of
# activity_logs.db, and a checkout of one of them destroyed a live 336-row
# database. token_usage.db has never been tracked, so nothing can overwrite it
# *today* — but that is an accident of history, not a property of the file, and
# it lapses silently the first time anyone commits it. Both files get the same
# rule so there is one thing to remember rather than a per-file exception.
#
# The cost is one line each in `git status`. .githooks/pre-commit is what keeps
# that harmless: enable it with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
#
# Sidecars stay ignored. They are transient, were never tracked, and would be
# pure noise; if a checkout ever threatens a database, the database itself is
# what makes git abort.
/activity_logs.db-wal
/activity_logs.db-shm
/token_usage.db-wal
/token_usage.db-shm

# Timestamped snapshots of both databases, taken by serve.py.
/backups/

__pycache__/

# The assembled website: site/ plus a copy of the dashboard exported from HEAD.
# Output, regenerated by site/build.py and published to gh-pages by
# site/publish.py. Note that site/assets/img/ is generated too but is NOT
# ignored — it is the landing page's content, and site/index.html has to open
# from a fresh clone with its images intact.
/site/_build/

# The reader's run report, written beside the usage cache and served to the
# source-transparency panel. Regenerated on every import.
/token_usage.report.json
